WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
video file & English subtitles: Safex

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:19.725
It's the first time for Terry
to be the leading actor.

00:00:20.404 --> 00:00:24.204
He reserved the best seat for Candy.

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:30.205
Susanna cried and asked Terry

00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:32.810
not to invite Candy.

00:00:35.519 --> 00:00:40.183
A love-shock therapy

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:46.456
Please, Terry.
Do you have to invite her?

00:00:46.997 --> 00:00:50.759
Susanna,
why are you so against Candy?

00:00:50.909 --> 00:00:53.530
Terry...

00:00:54.671 --> 00:00:58.600
I like you, Terry! I love you!

00:00:58.750 --> 00:00:59.869
Susanna...

00:01:00.777 --> 00:01:03.378
The first time I saw you, I...

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:12.387
Excuse me,
is this the Strasford Theatre?

00:01:13.857 --> 00:01:16.382
I am here for the acting test.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:23.691
I knew at that moment
that you would be chosen.

00:01:25.035 --> 00:01:29.031
After that, you played
a supporting role in King Lear.

00:01:29.181 --> 00:01:31.040
I was so happy!

00:01:31.608 --> 00:01:35.635
Standing on the stage with you,
I felt so blessed.

00:01:47.658 --> 00:01:50.586
I didn't care about the long trips.

00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:54.856
In your company, I always felt happy.

00:01:55.006 --> 00:01:57.957
Then Candy suddenly showed up
when we went to Chicago.

00:02:01.171 --> 00:02:03.581
You saw Candy? When?

00:02:03.731 --> 00:02:06.141
She came to the hotel, looking for you.

00:02:18.622 --> 00:02:21.284
I sent her back.

00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:28.220
I sent her away with lies.

00:02:32.235 --> 00:02:35.602
I understand you are angry.
You can blame me for everything!

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:43.805
I'm sorry! I know I made a mistake!

00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:47.247
I didn't want her
to steal your heart away.

00:02:47.551 --> 00:02:51.988
Tell me, your real feelings!

00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:59.488
I have always...

00:02:59.638 --> 00:03:01.053
Say no more!

00:03:02.132 --> 00:03:06.535
I will never give up my love for you!

00:03:06.837 --> 00:03:10.466
Whether it's Candy or anyone else!

00:03:11.208 --> 00:03:12.470
Susanna...

00:03:14.478 --> 00:03:16.446
I don't hate you.

00:03:17.347 --> 00:03:20.145
But my heart has always
been occupied by Candy alone.

00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:30.688
The first time I met her on the ship...

00:03:32.262 --> 00:03:36.289
It's true that I already fell in love
with her at that time.

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:40.962
My love for her will never change.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.210
Good morning!

00:03:53.416 --> 00:03:55.191
Let me do it.

00:03:55.341 --> 00:03:57.813
It's ok, go ahead and eat.
You are late for the hospital.

00:03:57.963 --> 00:04:00.482
Sorry I overslept.

00:04:00.857 --> 00:04:02.119
You seem like you didn't sleep well.

00:04:02.592 --> 00:04:04.186
I had nightmares.

00:04:04.336 --> 00:04:06.821
You called Terry's name
at least twenty to thirty times.

00:04:07.063 --> 00:04:08.724
Really?

00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:10.856
Just kidding.

00:04:12.235 --> 00:04:14.430
Mr. Albert is so naughty!

00:04:15.906 --> 00:04:17.399
I don't know what you dreamed.

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:21.137
Believe Terry.
He will send you that ticket.

00:04:21.845 --> 00:04:23.405
Of course I believe him!

00:04:23.555 --> 00:04:25.380
Ok, I give up!

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.845
Candy, look!

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:37.656
Patty!

00:04:39.596 --> 00:04:41.188
Is it her?

00:04:43.266 --> 00:04:44.790
Patty!

00:04:46.803 --> 00:04:49.567
What brought you here so early?

00:04:49.739 --> 00:04:51.333
I am here for you.

00:04:51.483 --> 00:04:52.898
For me?

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:56.471
Stear...

00:04:56.621 --> 00:04:58.776
What's wrong with Stear?

00:04:59.916 --> 00:05:02.885
He's going to war.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.442
To war?

00:05:05.592 --> 00:05:08.383
He's going to be a soldier.

00:05:08.533 --> 00:05:13.157
How would that be possible?
Stear can't even fight.

00:05:13.597 --> 00:05:17.158
Archie and Annie kept trying
to convince him to change his mind.

00:05:17.834 --> 00:05:20.029
But Stear just doesn't want to listen.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.064
I didn't think he would insist
so much on doing this.

00:05:23.214 --> 00:05:26.506
If you go talk to him,
maybe he will accept your opinion.

00:05:27.344 --> 00:05:30.575
Ok, I'll go at noon.

00:05:31.147 --> 00:05:34.548
Thank you, Candy!

00:05:35.752 --> 00:05:37.412
Your temperature is ok now.

00:05:37.562 --> 00:05:40.415
I want to leave here
to see my grandson.

00:05:40.565 --> 00:05:42.079
Your grandson?

00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:44.990
Yes. His name is Terry.

00:05:46.363 --> 00:05:47.796
Terry?

00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:51.332
Why are you all blushed?

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:55.565
He must be a good kid.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.735
Of course.

00:05:59.943 --> 00:06:02.070
What happened?

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.737
A fire?

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.273
Everyone, please stay calm.

00:06:10.287 --> 00:06:12.585
It's Stear!

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.489
Be quiet!

00:06:16.559 --> 00:06:18.925
Don't worry, everyone.

00:06:19.129 --> 00:06:21.290
It's alright. It'll be fixed soon.

00:06:22.332 --> 00:06:25.160
Sorry. It was usually ok.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.226
It broke
as soon as it got to the hospital.

00:06:27.771 --> 00:06:31.138
Stear, I heard
you want to join the army?

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:34.675
Who told you?

00:06:35.412 --> 00:06:38.040
Don't make Patty sad.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:42.575
Nosy!

00:06:43.586 --> 00:06:46.054
Patty is very worried about you.

00:06:47.257 --> 00:06:50.151
Candy, I made my decision.

00:06:50.301 --> 00:06:54.787
Stear, do you really understand
what war means?

00:06:55.565 --> 00:06:57.626
I read the newspapers.

00:06:57.776 --> 00:07:03.003
But Mr. Albert lost his memory
in the war.

00:07:03.773 --> 00:07:09.609
Some of the army nurses that
the hospital sent died in the war, too.

00:07:11.481 --> 00:07:15.281
More and more people will sacrifice
their lives in the war.

00:07:16.353 --> 00:07:17.479
Stear.

00:07:18.321 --> 00:07:20.382
If we don't stop the war,

00:07:20.532 --> 00:07:24.048
America will become a war zone one day.

00:07:24.198 --> 00:07:25.593
America?

00:07:28.865 --> 00:07:32.858
I have to fight the war in Europe
to prevent this.

00:07:35.105 --> 00:07:37.262
Why it must be you?

00:07:37.412 --> 00:07:38.566
Candy.

00:07:38.716 --> 00:07:42.337
You want me to hide here
to invent some stupid things,

00:07:42.487 --> 00:07:44.880
and live an easy life?

00:07:45.181 --> 00:07:46.580
Of course not.

00:07:47.283 --> 00:07:49.513
I am not afraid of death.

00:07:50.253 --> 00:07:51.880
Good-bye.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:55.648
Stear!

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.628
Patty...

00:08:06.836 --> 00:08:08.663
Patty, everything will be fine.

00:08:08.813 --> 00:08:11.400
I don't want to lose Stear!

00:08:12.108 --> 00:08:13.837
I don't want him to fight in the war!

00:08:16.946 --> 00:08:21.476
Maybe Mr. Albert can convince Stear!

00:08:21.626 --> 00:08:23.382
But, Mr. Albert...

00:08:24.387 --> 00:08:27.989
I have to try to help him
regain his memory.

00:08:31.628 --> 00:08:33.892
Treatments for amnesia...

00:08:37.167 --> 00:08:40.364
One way of treatment
is to shock the patient.

00:08:41.504 --> 00:08:43.938
I got it, the shock treatment!

00:08:54.217 --> 00:08:55.616
I'm back!

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.484
It didn't scare him at all.

00:09:04.828 --> 00:09:06.894
Kids' trick!

00:09:15.138 --> 00:09:16.765
It has to be successful this time!

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.841
Mr. Albert, can you help me?

00:09:20.643 --> 00:09:21.701
No problem.

00:09:22.979 --> 00:09:25.470
I am going to set the table.

00:09:25.949 --> 00:09:27.576
Strange...

00:09:28.218 --> 00:09:30.516
What do we have for dinner?

00:09:40.363 --> 00:09:43.487
Candy, are we having popcorn for dinner?

00:09:43.637 --> 00:09:45.430
Still not responding...

00:09:45.602 --> 00:09:48.229
Have a seat first.

00:09:48.379 --> 00:09:49.531
What's going on?

00:09:49.681 --> 00:09:51.665
Sit down first.

00:10:00.383 --> 00:10:01.576
Ouch!

00:10:01.726 --> 00:10:04.112
I'm sorry, Mr. Albert!

00:10:04.262 --> 00:10:06.642
I want to help you regain your memory.

00:10:06.792 --> 00:10:08.815
The sound of a train.

00:10:09.926 --> 00:10:13.157
I hear the sound of a train in my head.

00:10:15.331 --> 00:10:19.461
The train  that Mr. Albert took,
that was attacked and exploded.

00:10:20.904 --> 00:10:23.532
Mr. Albert is remembering it.

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:36.314
Sorry, I've gone too far.

00:10:36.519 --> 00:10:38.646
No, my head is hurting so much!

00:10:39.122 --> 00:10:42.614
The things happened in the train,
you can remember them now?

00:10:42.992 --> 00:10:45.586
No, just the sound.

00:10:45.828 --> 00:10:47.921
You just heard the sound?

00:10:49.365 --> 00:10:51.255
And other sounds, too.

00:10:56.539 --> 00:10:58.473
I hear them too!

00:11:06.382 --> 00:11:07.876
Mr. Albert, there is a fire!

00:11:08.026 --> 00:11:09.475
Candy, the window!

00:11:14.424 --> 00:11:17.086
It's Stear's car!

00:11:17.827 --> 00:11:19.124
Is it...

00:11:19.529 --> 00:11:20.894
That smoke...

00:11:25.001 --> 00:11:26.400
Stear!

00:11:29.339 --> 00:11:30.865
- What's going on?
- Nothing.

00:11:31.015 --> 00:11:32.601
It's just an experiment.

00:11:34.544 --> 00:11:35.977
Idiot!

00:11:38.448 --> 00:11:41.144
My Rider One!

00:11:46.055 --> 00:11:50.185
I see. You are trying to help
Mr. Albert regain his memory.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:54.889
The book said that recreating
the setting at the memory loss time

00:11:55.039 --> 00:11:59.628
is helpful for restoration, so I...

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:03.161
I told you to stop!

00:12:04.307 --> 00:12:07.936
Listen! I'll get you evicted
if you ever make trouble again!

00:12:09.445 --> 00:12:11.034
I'm really sorry about it.

00:12:11.184 --> 00:12:12.704
We'll pay attention next time.

00:12:15.618 --> 00:12:18.314
Please forgive the trouble.

00:12:18.988 --> 00:12:21.730
Are you saying
that you did something, too?

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:24.588
No! I am going to go make some tea.

00:12:29.465 --> 00:12:30.796
Thank you

00:12:31.267 --> 00:12:33.531
for caring about my health.

00:12:34.304 --> 00:12:36.097
No, I...

00:12:36.247 --> 00:12:40.506
I hope you can convince Stear
not to go to the front line.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:43.004
My brother needs a favour from you.

00:12:43.154 --> 00:12:44.938
What is it?

00:12:45.088 --> 00:12:50.212
I hope Mr. Albert can help me
convince Grand Aunt Elroy.

00:12:50.453 --> 00:12:54.412
Grand Aunt Elroy is against
Stear joining the army.

00:12:54.691 --> 00:12:55.953
Of course!

00:12:56.192 --> 00:12:59.992
Mr. Albert must understand my feelings.

00:13:01.431 --> 00:13:03.899
Stear, I am afraid I will let you down.

00:13:04.133 --> 00:13:08.069
Right. Who would want you
to fight in the war?

00:13:08.971 --> 00:13:11.030
The Mr. Albert now
may not agree with me.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:15.803
If Mr. Albert regains his memory,
he will support me.

00:13:15.953 --> 00:13:17.368
How could this be possible?

00:13:18.047 --> 00:13:20.475
There are few doctors in Africa.

00:13:20.625 --> 00:13:24.782
Didn't Mr. Albert take part in that, too?

00:13:25.288 --> 00:13:30.055
What I am thinking now, is just like
what Mr. Albert was thinking then.

00:13:34.664 --> 00:13:37.389
I was a doctor in Africa?

00:13:37.539 --> 00:13:41.094
You will understand me
when you have your memory back.

00:13:43.272 --> 00:13:44.198
Candy.

00:13:44.348 --> 00:13:47.367
Can you understand why
brother pretended there was a fire?

00:13:48.611 --> 00:13:49.971
I see.

00:13:50.121 --> 00:13:55.150
We all want to help Mr. Albert,
with different purposes.

00:14:03.726 --> 00:14:06.957
The war occupies Stear's mind now.

00:14:07.363 --> 00:14:10.922
He only wants to go to the frontline.

00:14:12.402 --> 00:14:15.229
Patty, calm down!

00:14:15.379 --> 00:14:18.330
Let's have a picnic
for our next vacation.

00:14:18.741 --> 00:14:21.803
Thank you,
but I am not in the mood right now.

00:14:21.953 --> 00:14:27.612
Patty, do you still remember
the summer school in Scotland?

00:14:31.554 --> 00:14:36.150
We were without worry,
spending each day happily.

00:14:57.079 --> 00:14:58.542
It's breaking down!

00:14:59.449 --> 00:15:01.041
Brother, is it alright?

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.184
Stear, come on!

00:15:04.387 --> 00:15:05.413
There is no other way.

00:15:05.563 --> 00:15:08.184
The girls stay in the car,
the boys push the car.

00:15:08.658 --> 00:15:09.950
Leave it to me!

00:15:10.726 --> 00:15:12.553
Archie, Mr. Albert.

00:15:12.703 --> 00:15:14.528
Boys should get off and push the van.

00:15:17.033 --> 00:15:20.594
Candy,
do you really think you are a boy?

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.895
Oops!

00:15:23.639 --> 00:15:25.732
Thanks for the work, Mr. Albert.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:39.914
I prepared some cocoa.

00:15:40.064 --> 00:15:42.150
Let me peel the apples.

00:15:44.026 --> 00:15:45.687
I'll help.

00:15:46.195 --> 00:15:48.686
You should take a rest once in a while.

00:15:49.899 --> 00:15:54.893
Once in a while?
Mr. Albert cooks most of the time?

00:15:55.671 --> 00:15:57.298
Oops!

00:15:58.541 --> 00:16:01.402
Mr. Albert is feeling better.

00:16:01.552 --> 00:16:05.709
Doesn't look like the patient
from ward No. 0.

00:16:10.219 --> 00:16:14.128
With such a nice weather and scenery,
anyone would want to stay alive.

00:16:15.858 --> 00:16:19.555
Candy, thank you
for everything you've done to me.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.229
This is good enough.

00:16:22.465 --> 00:16:25.525
Mr. Albert, the lunch is ready!

00:16:25.801 --> 00:16:28.329
Stear, hurry!
The cocoa is getting cold!

00:16:28.479 --> 00:16:30.612
I am coming!

00:16:30.762 --> 00:16:31.934
Thanks.

00:16:34.844 --> 00:16:36.141
Candy.

00:16:36.312 --> 00:16:40.078
I have a new invention. Watch.

00:16:49.458 --> 00:16:51.050
Stear, what are you doing?

00:16:59.168 --> 00:17:00.928
Mr. Albert, how do you feel?

00:17:01.078 --> 00:17:03.498
The is a memory restoration machine
that I invented.

00:17:03.648 --> 00:17:05.561
Nonsense, Stear!

00:17:05.711 --> 00:17:09.166
This is made by rubber,
it won't hurt.

00:17:09.979 --> 00:17:13.437
It has a trick here.
It will jump off when pressed.

00:17:14.016 --> 00:17:16.177
Just the noise is kind of loud.

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:21.616
My head is not hurting,
but my butt is.

00:17:22.758 --> 00:17:24.555
Sorry, Mr. Albert.

00:17:26.529 --> 00:17:29.726
Candy has tried already
the shock treatment.

00:17:31.033 --> 00:17:33.365
Candy does violent stuff, too?

00:17:33.669 --> 00:17:37.969
No... I...

00:17:38.541 --> 00:17:40.065
Patty.

00:17:40.476 --> 00:17:42.239
You eat first.

00:17:43.412 --> 00:17:47.642
Stear, you are thinking about the war
even on a picnic!

00:17:47.792 --> 00:17:48.979
Patty!

00:17:54.256 --> 00:17:55.294
Patty.

00:17:55.444 --> 00:17:58.552
We are supposed to be happy today.

00:17:59.462 --> 00:18:01.322
I...

00:18:01.472 --> 00:18:03.524
Patty, it will be fine.

00:18:03.674 --> 00:18:07.207
Mr. Albert wouldn't encourage Stear
to go to war,

00:18:07.357 --> 00:18:09.964
even if he would have back his memory.

00:18:10.172 --> 00:18:11.969
You don't need to worry about it.

00:18:12.441 --> 00:18:13.965
Everyone is waiting for you.

00:18:16.479 --> 00:18:18.947
Come on, let's go back!

00:18:22.451 --> 00:18:23.744
Mr. Thomas?

00:18:23.894 --> 00:18:27.016
Patty, I'll be right back,
you can go first.

00:18:28.724 --> 00:18:30.248
Mr. Thomas!

00:18:35.931 --> 00:18:40.227
My wife and my son
are buried on the hill.

00:18:40.377 --> 00:18:42.566
You came to sweep the tomb?

00:18:45.941 --> 00:18:50.207
I saw them burn to death.

00:18:50.579 --> 00:18:53.207
It was twenty years ago,

00:18:53.683 --> 00:18:57.244
but it feels like yesterday.

00:18:58.688 --> 00:19:01.020
I often wake up
in the middle of the night.

00:19:02.058 --> 00:19:07.155
Sometimes, I envy Mr. Albert so much.

00:19:08.664 --> 00:19:10.359
Because he lost his memory?

00:19:11.133 --> 00:19:12.860
Mr. Albert lost his memory

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:17.736
because he didn't want
to remember the pain in the past.

00:19:19.241 --> 00:19:23.678
You tried so hard to help him.

00:19:24.046 --> 00:19:26.574
Once he is recovered,

00:19:26.724 --> 00:19:30.278
all the bad memories will come back too.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.714
Mr. Thomas is right.

00:19:33.864 --> 00:19:35.516
All that we do

00:19:35.666 --> 00:19:38.287
may only make it
more painful for Mr. Albert.

00:19:39.295 --> 00:19:40.887
Good afternoon, Mr. Thomas.

00:19:41.363 --> 00:19:42.523
Stay with us for meal.

00:19:42.673 --> 00:19:46.622
No, thanks. You are...

00:19:46.772 --> 00:19:49.060
We see each other every morning.

00:19:49.772 --> 00:19:51.501
It really is you!

00:19:52.341 --> 00:19:53.968
Every morning?

00:19:58.414 --> 00:20:02.612
I go to church every morning,

00:20:03.085 --> 00:20:06.447
to pray for my daughter's safety
in Italy.

00:20:06.597 --> 00:20:10.515
Patty prays for Stear every day?

00:20:16.298 --> 00:20:20.166
It doesn't matter
if Stear hates me or not.

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:23.395
I only hope you can stay alive.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:25.300
Patty!

00:20:27.743 --> 00:20:30.876
Stear, I am actually half alive.

00:20:31.781 --> 00:20:33.841
Before, how did I spend my days?

00:20:33.991 --> 00:20:37.408
How did I think?
I don't remember either of them.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:42.848
But of one thing I am sure about.

00:20:43.692 --> 00:20:46.160
Even if I regained my memory,

00:20:46.896 --> 00:20:50.832
I wouldn't support your decision
to go to war

00:20:52.968 --> 00:20:54.401
Mr. Albert...

00:20:57.673 --> 00:21:00.301
He seems to be recovering.

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:07.005
Stear starts to wonder
if his decision is right.

00:21:08.083 --> 00:21:11.519
Seeing Patty and Stear
getting back together

00:21:11.821 --> 00:21:15.349
makes Candy want to fly to Broadway
right now,

